From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: explorer: no taskbar button for a tool window

On Windows a WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW window gets no taskbar button unless it also
has WS_EX_APPWINDOW. Explorer's taskbar gave every unowned window one, so
the Start menu, flyouts and other tool windows showed up as buttons.

Gate: test/vdesk-gate.sh (a tool window beside two windows: two buttons).
---
--- a/programs/explorer/systray.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/systray.c
@@ -856,7 +856,10 @@
         }
         win->active = (win->hwnd == foreground);
         /* Stained Glass OS: only the current virtual desktop's windows */
+        /* as on Windows: no button for a tool window (Start, flyouts), unless
+         * it asks for one with WS_EX_APPWINDOW */
         win->visible = IsWindowVisible( win->hwnd ) && !GetWindow( win->hwnd, GW_OWNER ) &&
+                       ((GetWindowLongW( win->hwnd, GWL_EXSTYLE ) & (WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW | WS_EX_APPWINDOW)) != WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW) &&
                        vd_on_current( win->hwnd );
         if (win->visible) count++;
     }
